{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ve been reviewing why you came in. You had three episodes of vomiting blood last night, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:29:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up with this fullness in my stomach and then vomited a cup of blood. Then twice more—each time about a cup. I felt dizzy after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You also mentioned sharp pain in your upper belly that goes to your back. How bad is it now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:32:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s throbbing, still pretty bad. I’ve been on Dilaudid at home, but it’s not helping as much as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you fluids and medication in the ER. Your labs show your hemoglobin dropped a bit, but it’s likely from the fluids diluting your blood, not ongoing bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I *was* bleeding, right? Why can’t we find the source?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:36:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did bleed, but your NG tube wash came back clean, and your stool test was negative for blood. Also, you had an EGD just eight days ago—no active bleeding was seen then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:37:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what caused it? Could it be my lupus? Or the pancreatitis they used to say I had?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lupus is being treated with prednisone and methotrexate, which we’ll continue. But imaging hasn’t shown chronic pancreatitis. The bleeding might be from a Mallory-Weiss tear—small tears from vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had so many tests. Why can’t we figure this out? I’m scared it’ll happen again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:42:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ve done a lot—EGDs, CT scans, capsule endoscopy—all normal except for a small hiatal hernia and some duodenal atrophy. Nothing explains the pain or bleeding clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My mom is worried we’re not doing enough. And you couldn’t find Dr. ___’s recent notes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-06-18 04:45:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We see you’ve seen him recently, but his notes aren’t in our system. We’re trying to get them. In the meantime, we’re following your usual meds and monitoring you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on clear liquids. You vomited apple juice earlier—no blood. That’s a good sign. How’s your pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there. I just want to go home. I can manage my pain meds there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’d prefer you stay a bit longer to make sure you can keep food down and your levels stabilize. But I understand you want to leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do. I’ll follow up with my PCP and Dr. ___. Can I go home now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it’s against medical advice. We recommend bowel rest, advance diet slowly, and return if you vomit blood, can’t keep fluids down, or feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. I’ll watch for those signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending you home on your usual meds. Prednisone is now 10 mg three times a day. Continue the Nexium and Zofran as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my Dilaudid for pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:27:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 2 mg every four hours as needed. Also, we added stool softeners in case the pain meds cause constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll call my doctor tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. If symptoms worsen, go to the ER. We care about your safety, even if you’re leaving AMA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. I just need to be at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve arranged for discharge. A nurse will go over instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-06-18 05:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Please follow up soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-06-18 04:28:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-06-18 12:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of systemic lupus erythematosus, chronic abdominal pain, and recurrent hematemesis presented with three episodes of vomiting blood and severe epigastric pain radiating to the back. She had undergone an EGD eight days prior with no acute bleeding source identified. In the emergency department, nasogastric lavage was negative and stool was heme-negative, suggesting no active gastrointestinal hemorrhage. She was admitted for observation, started on IV fluids and medications including a proton pump inhibitor and anti-nausea treatment, and advanced to clear liquids. Despite medical recommendations to remain hospitalized, she requested discharge against medical advice due to dissatisfaction with pain control and concerns about missing specialist notes. She was discharged home with instructions to advance her diet cautiously, continue her home medications including prednisone and methotrexate, and seek immediate care if symptoms worsened.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Hematemesis",
      "Systemic lupus erythematosus",
      "Postural tachycardia syndrome",
      "Depression"
    ]
  }
}
